9, 'node_id': 'IC_kwDODlDwxc5q5EtL', 'user': {'login': 'knausj85', 'id': 15005956, 'node_id': 'MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDA1OTU2', 'avatar_url': 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15005956?v=4', 'gravatar_id': '', 'url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/knausj85', 'followers_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/followers', 'following_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/following{/other_user}', 'gists_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/gists{/gist_id}', 'starred_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/starred{/owner}{/repo}', 'subscriptions_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/subscriptions', 'organizations_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/orgs', 'repos_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/repos', 'events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/events{/privacy}', 'received_events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/knausj85/received_events', 'type': 'User', 'user_view_type': 'public', 'site_admin': False}, 'created_at': '2023-11-04T05:20:52Z', 'updated_at': '2023-11-04T05:27:06Z', 'body': "> Hmm I'm struggling to see how this belongs in community. This code is all very Cursorless-specific

Since it's guarded by the cursorless tag, I'm not opposed to including this functionality. I think the power of the feature is significant enough to justify including it.

Is there any alternative -- support within cursorless itself?

Edit:

Actually I suppose the cursorless tag won't exist without the extension installed and may cause some log spam. may not be ideal.", 'author_association': 'MEMBER', 'pin': None, 'reactions': {'url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/comments/1793346379/reactions', 'total_count': 0, '+1': 0, '-1': 0, 'laugh': 0, 'hooray': 0, 'confused': 0, 'heart': 0, 'rocket': 0, 'eyes': 0}, 'performed_via_github_app': None}, {'url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/comments/1793369833', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/talonhub/community/pull/1305#issuecomment-1793369833', 'issue_url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/1305', 'id': 1793369833, 'node_id': 'IC_kwDODlDwxc5q5Kbp', 'user': {'login': 'AndreasArvidsson', 'id': 3511326, 'node_id': 'MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTEzMjY=', 'avatar_url': 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3511326?v=4', 'gravatar_id': '', 'url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/AndreasArvidsson', 'followers_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/followers', 'following_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/following{/other_user}', 'gists_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/gists{/gist_id}', 'starred_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}', 'subscriptions_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/subscriptions', 'organizations_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/orgs', 'repos_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/repos', 'events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/events{/privacy}', 'received_events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/received_events', 'type': 'User', 'user_view_type': 'public', 'site_admin': False}, 'created_at': '2023-11-04T07:26:29Z', 'updated_at': '2023-11-04T07:30:57Z', 'body': "cThis feature requires 1 list that only exist in community, it requires 2 actions that only exists community and it requires 1 dataclass that only exists in community. On the other side the Cursorless snippet api and the Cursorless target capture feels much more public and stable.

There is only really two lines that are Cursorless specific. The one with the targets capture and calling the insert action. If we want to support wrapper snippets in different editors in the future it's much better to have the communality in community.

I've already added the Cursorless tag to community so we shouldn't have any warnings in the log. Defining a tag twice also doesn't seem to be any problem in Talon.", 'author_association': 'COLLABORATOR', 'pin': None, 'reactions': {'url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/comments/1793369833/reactions', 'total_count': 0, '+1': 0, '-1': 0, 'laugh': 0, 'hooray': 0, 'confused': 0, 'heart': 0, 'rocket': 0, 'eyes': 0}, 'performed_via_github_app': None}, {'url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/comments/1793381527', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/talonhub/community/pull/1305#issuecomment-1793381527', 'issue_url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/1305', 'id': 1793381527, 'node_id': 'IC_kwDODlDwxc5q5NSX', 'user': {'login': 'lunixbochs', 'id': 117642, 'node_id': 'MDQ6VXNlcjExNzY0Mg==', 'avatar_url': 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/117642?v=4', 'gravatar_id': '', 'url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/lunixbochs', 'followers_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/followers', 'following_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/following{/other_user}', 'gists_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/gists{/gist_id}', 'starred_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/starred{/owner}{/repo}', 'subscriptions_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/subscriptions', 'organizations_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/orgs', 'repos_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/repos', 'events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/events{/privacy}', 'received_events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/lunixbochs/received_events', 'type': 'User', 'user_view_type': 'public', 'site_admin': False}, 'created_at': '2023-11-04T08:26:46Z', 'updated_at': '2023-11-04T08:26:46Z', 'body': 'Defining something on two mods may become an error, the current behavior of ignoring one of them at random is incidental and not stable', 'author_association': 'COLLABORATOR', 'pin': None, 'reactions': {'url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/comments/1793381527/reactions', 'total_count': 0, '+1': 0, '-1': 0, 'laugh': 0, 'hooray': 0, 'confused': 0, 'heart': 0, 'rocket': 0, 'eyes': 0}, 'performed_via_github_app': None}, {'url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/comments/1793408882', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/talonhub/community/pull/1305#issuecomment-1793408882', 'issue_url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/1305', 'id': 1793408882, 'node_id': 'IC_kwDODlDwxc5q5T9y', 'user': {'login': 'AndreasArvidsson', 'id': 3511326, 'node_id': 'MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTEzMjY=', 'avatar_url': 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3511326?v=4', 'gravatar_id': '', 'url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/AndreasArvidsson', 'followers_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/followers', 'following_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/following{/other_user}', 'gists_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/gists{/gist_id}', 'starred_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/starred{/owner}{/repo}', 'subscriptions_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/subscriptions', 'organizations_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/orgs', 'repos_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/repos', 'events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/events{/privacy}', 'received_events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/AndreasArvidsson/received_events', 'type': 'User', 'user_view_type': 'public', 'site_admin': False}, 'created_at': '2023-11-04T10:42:13Z', 'updated_at': '2023-11-04T10:47:20Z', 'body': "Okay then we'll rethink this. 
My current solution is to add things in both community and Cursorless to minimize the dependencies between them

* Community retains all information about the snippet dataclass and its features
* Community declares an action to insert wrapper snippets with no implementation/body 
* Cursorless implements the above action on a Cursorless specific context
* Cursorless adds a voice command

I'm quite happy with this solution. The only real downside is that Cursorless needs to know about the community list. Aside from that the separation is quite good.

https://github.com/cursorless-dev/cursorless/pull/1998
