.com/talonhub/community/pull/786#issuecomment-1065900330', 'issue_url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/786', 'id': 1065900330, 'node_id': 'IC_kwDODlDwxc4_iFkq', 'user': {'login': 'pokey', 'id': 755842, 'node_id': 'MDQ6VXNlcjc1NTg0Mg==', 'avatar_url': 'https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/755842?v=4', 'gravatar_id': '', 'url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey', 'html_url': 'https://github.com/pokey', 'followers_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/followers', 'following_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/following{/other_user}', 'gists_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/gists{/gist_id}', 'starred_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/starred{/owner}{/repo}', 'subscriptions_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/subscriptions', 'organizations_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/orgs', 'repos_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/repos', 'events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/events{/privacy}', 'received_events_url': 'https://api.github.com/users/pokey/received_events', 'type': 'User', 'user_view_type': 'public', 'site_admin': False}, 'created_at': '2022-03-12T15:15:23Z', 'updated_at': '2022-03-12T15:15:23Z', 'body': '@RyanRuane the below is not a blocking request, but fwiw I'd be inclined to go a step further wrt the macro / function thing, and just have a single command "funk" that you use for functions, square macros, curly macros etc, and then have separate sets that you can use to indicate things that want square or curly brackets.  Something like the following:

```python
square_bracket_macros = {
    "vec!",
}

curly_bracket_macros = {
    "foo!",
    "bar!",
}
```

Then in `code_insert_function`, do something like

```python
    def code_insert_function(text: str, selection: str):
        if text in square_bracket_macros:
            code_insert_function_or_macro(text, selection, '[', ']')
        elif text in curly_bracket_macros:
            code_insert_function_or_macro(text, selection, '{', '}')
        else:
            code_insert_function_or_macro(text, selection, '(', ')')
```

This approach presumes you'll always use the same style brackets with the same macro, but if so, it's one less thing to think about while coding.  You just always say "funk foo", and don't need to worry about function vs macro / bracket style / etc.  As @rntz mentions, the less you have to think about while voice coding the better', 'author_association': 'COLLABORATOR', 'pin': None, 'reactions': {'url': 'https://api.github.com/repos/talonhub/community/issues/comments/1065900330/reactions', 'total_count': 0, '+1': 0, '-1': 0, 'laugh': 0, 'hooray': 0, 'confused': 0, 'heart': 0, 'rocket': 0, 'eyes': 0}, 'performed_via_github_app': None}]
